# Implementation Plan: AURA Product Roadmap

## Overview

This implementation plan follows the 8-phase roadmap for AURA (AI-powered personal stylist). The plan is organized by sprint, with each sprint building on previous foundations. All tasks use TypeScript with React for the frontend and Node.js/Express for the backend.

**MVP Focus (Sprints 1-3):** The core MVP requires Sprints 1-3 to establish:
- Wardrobe management with persistence
- Basic AI clothing recognition
- Outfit generation with compatibility scoring
- Shopping intelligence (duplicate detection, buy recommendations)
- Analytics dashboard

---

## Phase 1: Foundation & Wardrobe Management (Sprint 1)

### Sprint 1.1: Project Structure and Backend Setup

- [ ] 1.1.1 Set up backend project structure
  - Create Express server with TypeScript configuration
  - Set up folder structure: `src/api`, `src/services`, `src/persistence`, `src/middleware`
  - Configure `.env` file for API keys
  - _Requirements: 33, 34, 35_

- [ ] 1.1.2 Implement data persistence layer
  - Create `src/persistence/database.ts` with JSON file I/O
  - Implement atomic write operations (temp file + rename)
  - Add in-memory caching with LRU strategy
  - _Requirements: 3, 5_

- [ ] 1.1.3 Create initial API routes and middleware
  - Set up Express server with middleware stack
  - Implement request validation middleware
  - Add error handling and logging
  - _Requirements: 33, 35_

- [ ] 1.1.4 Write unit tests for persistence layer
  - Test file read/write operations
  - Test cache behavior
  - _Requirements: 3_

- [ ]* 1.1.5 Write integration tests for API routes
  - Test endpoint responses
  - Test error handling
  - _Requirements: 33, 34, 35_

### Sprint 1.2: Wardrobe CRUD Operations

- [ ] 1.2.1 Implement WardrobeItem type definitions
  - Create TypeScript interfaces for `WardrobeItem`
  - Define category, condition, and type enums
  - _Requirements: 5_

- [ ] 1.2.2 Implement wardrobe CRUD endpoints
  - `GET /api/wardrobe` - List all items
  - `GET /api/wardrobe/:id` - Get single item
  - `POST /api/wardrobe` - Create new item
  - `PATCH /api/wardrobe/:id` - Update item
  - `DELETE /api/wardrobe/:id` - Delete item
  - _Requirements: 3, 7, 8_

- [ ] 1.2.3 Implement item persistence logic
  - Add item with auto-generated ID and timestamps
  - Update item preserving ID and updating timestamps
  - Delete item with cascade checks for outfit references
  - _Requirements: 3, 7, 8_

- [ ] 1.2.4 Create API service layer
  - Implement business logic for CRUD operations
  - Add validation rules for item fields
  - _Requirements: 5, 7_

- [ ] 1.2.5 Write unit tests for CRUD operations
  - Test create, read, update, delete scenarios
  - Test validation edge cases
  - _Requirements: 3, 5, 7, 8_

- [ ]* 1.2.6 Write integration tests for wardrobe endpoints
  - Test full CRUD workflow
  - Test error scenarios
  - _Requirements: 3, 5, 7, 8_

### Sprint 1.3: Visual Wardrobe Display

- [ ] 1.3.1 Create wardrobe React components
  - `WardrobeGrid` - Main grid container component
  - `WardrobeCard` - Individual item card with image
  - `EmptyState` - Empty wardrobe placeholder
  - _Requirements: 6_

- [ ] 1.3.2 Implement responsive grid layout
  - Mobile: 2-column grid (320px-767px)
  - Tablet: 3-column grid (768px-1023px)
  - Desktop: 4-column grid (1024px+)
  - _Requirements: 31_

- [ ] 1.3.3 Add image placeholders and loading states
  - Create skeleton loading components
  - Implement lazy loading for images
  - _Requirements: 6_

- [ ] 1.3.4 Connect frontend to backend API
  - Implement API service for wardrobe operations
  - Add error handling and retry logic
  - _Requirements: 36_

- [ ] 1.3.5 Write unit tests for wardrobe components
  - Test rendering with sample data
  - Test empty state
  - _Requirements: 6_

- [ ]* 1.3.6 Write visual regression tests
  - Test responsive layouts on different screen sizes
  - _Requirements: 31_

