## Phase 2: AI Clothing Recognition (Sprint 2)

### Sprint 2.1: AI Integration Setup

- [ ] 2.1.1 Install and configure Google GenAI SDK
  - Install `@google/genai` package
  - Create AI service configuration
  - Add environment variable for API key
  - _Requirements: 9_

- [ ] 2.1.2 Create AI service client
  - Implement `src/services/aiClient.ts`
  - Configure Gemini model (gemini-2.5-flash)
  - Add request/response logging for debugging
  - _Requirements: 9, 10_

- [ ] 2.1.3 Implement retry logic and error handling
  - Add exponential backoff for API failures
  - Implement fallback to default values
  - _Requirements: 37_

### Sprint 2.2: Image Analysis Integration

- [ ] 2.2.1 Implement garment image analysis endpoint
  - `POST /api/analyze-wardrobe-image` endpoint
  - Accept Base64-encoded image data
  - Send to Gemini Vision API
  - _Requirements: 9_

- [ ] 2.2.2 Parse and validate AI response
  - Create TypeScript interface for `AnalyzedGarmentResult`
  - Extract detected fields: category, color, pattern, material, formality
  - Validate confidence scores
  - _Requirements: 9, 10_

- [ ] 2.2.3 Implement confidence threshold logic
  - Flag low-confidence fields (< 0.70)
  - Highlight fields for user review
  - Provide manual override options
  - _Requirements: 9, 10_

- [ ] 2.2.4 Create image upload UI component
  - File input with drag-and-drop
  - Image preview before upload
  - Progress indicator
  - _Requirements: 4, 31_

- [ ] 2.2.5 Write unit tests for AI integration
  - Test API call with mocked responses
  - Test response parsing
  - Test fallback behavior
  - _Requirements: 9_

- [ ]* 2.2.6 Write integration tests for image analysis
  - Test complete upload and analysis flow
  - Test error scenarios (no image, low quality)
  - _Requirements: 9, 10_

### Sprint 2.3: User Correction System

- [ ] 2.3.1 Create item editing modal
  - Display AI suggestions alongside editable fields
  - Highlight changed fields with visual indicators
  - _Requirements: 10_

- [ ] 2.3.2 Implement user edit persistence
  - Merge user edits with AI suggestions
  - Preserve user input over AI suggestions
  - Update item in database
  - _Requirements: 10_

- [ ] 2.3.3 Add correction logging
  - Log user corrections for model improvement
  - Store correction metadata (timestamp, user ID)
  - _Requirements: 10_

- [ ] 2.3.4 Write unit tests for editing logic
  - Test correction merging
  - Test validation after correction
  - _Requirements: 10_

